+# gen_e2e
+
+End-to-end proof app for `fuse add` / `fuse gen` (generated Flutter interop).
+Findings: `experiments/interop/reports/06-e2e-fuse-add.md`.
+
+What is in here:
+
+- `fuse.config.ts`: the `native` allow-list (Flutter SDK widgets + `percent_indicator`).
+- `dart/lib/fuse/rating_badge.dart`: a plain Flutter widget, the escape hatch. No FuseNode code.
+- `src/_generated/`, `dart/lib/_generated/`, `fuse.lock`: written by `fuse gen`, committed.
+- `src/index.tsx`: uses the generated wrappers; `src/ui/gauge.tsx` is a hand-written JS layer over one.
+- `dart/integration_test/generated_widgets_test.dart`: drives the real pipeline on Linux desktop.
+
+```bash
+export PATH=/opt/flutter/bin:$PATH
+bun install                      # at the repo root
+(cd ../../packages/solid-fuse && bun run build)
+
+bun fuse gen                     # regenerate (about 30 s: analyzer cold start)
+bun fuse gen --check             # exit 1 when generated output is stale
+bun fuse catalog RatingBadge     # one widget: props, defaults, docs
+bunx tsc --noEmit
+
+# the proof: build the bundle with dev validators, run it in a real Flutter app under xvfb
+bun fuse build --js-only --dev
+(cd dart && xvfb-run -a flutter test integration_test/generated_widgets_test.dart -d linux)
+```
+
+(`bun fuse` runs `node_modules/.bin/fuse`, which is `packages/solid-fuse/cli/index.ts`.)
